            <div xml:id="d749-a5">

                <pb facs="0926" n="824" sameAs="frus:frus1908/pg824"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 5.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Chargé Sleeper to the
                            French Vice Consul, guardian of the archives of the
                            French Legation.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Caracas</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1908-06-20"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">June 20,
                    1908</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to inform you that the Government of
                    the United States has decided to close its legation in Caracas and to place its
                    interests, property, and archives, in Venezuela, in the hands of the
                    representative of Brazil.</p>
                <p>I have to add that I have this day notified the minister for foreign affairs to
                    this effect, and requested my passports.</p>
                <p>No instructions regarding French interests have been received by this
                    legation.</p>
                <p>Very respectfully,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Jacob Sleeper.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
